 "segments": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 7.16,
   "t": "the gentlest nurse on the ward, and America's most prolific killer, Autumn of 2003, at Somerset"
  },
  {
   "s": 7.16,
   "e": 12.26,
   "t": "Medical Center in Somerville, New Jersey. The 43-year-old man possessed a frail frame,"
  },
  {
   "s": 12.68,
   "e": 17.14,
   "t": "spoke in a quiet murmur, always greeted colleagues with a gentle smile, and eagerly"
  },
  {
   "s": 17.14,
   "e": 22.18,
   "t": "volunteered to cover shifts for exhausted co-workers. Yet, beneath that pristine white"
  },
  {
   "s": 22.18,
   "e": 27.52,
   "t": "scrubs lay a lethal halo effect that concealed a terrifying psychological abyss for 16 long"
  },
  {
   "s": 27.52,
   "e": 32.6,
   "t": "years. He was always the first to rush in whenever a patient deteriorated and quietly"
  },
  {
   "s": 32.6,
   "e": 35.84,
   "t": "stayed behind to tidy up the room after failed resuscitations."
  },
  {
   "s": 36.72,
   "e": 42.14,
   "t": "All of us nurses at Somerset Medical Center, Charlie was simply an incredible friend. He"
  },
  {
   "s": 42.14,
   "e": 46.86,
   "t": "was considerate, never lost his temper, and cared for patients with exceptional gentleness."
  },
  {
   "s": 47.68,
   "e": 52.14,
   "t": "Until the truth broke open, all of us felt a chill down our spines upon realizing"
  },
  {
   "s": 52.14,
   "e": 56.14,
   "t": "we had worked alongside one of the most prolific serial killers in history."
  }
 ]
}